# SentinelX — Cursor Guardrails

Full context: `.kiro/steering/sentinelx.md` (source of truth). This file is a
condensed operational checklist — if anything here seems to conflict with the
steering doc, the steering doc wins. When in doubt, STOP and ask, don't guess.

## Rule #0
Do not try to impress the project owner. Build exactly what the ticket
specifies. If a task would require changing architecture, the data model,
the pipeline, or V1 scope — STOP and ask for approval. Never mark a ticket
DONE yourself; that's the developer's call.

## Scope — V1 NetLab only
- ZERO AI imports (openai, groq, anthropic, google.generativeai)
- NO REST API, NO GUI, NO user accounts, NO auto-fix, NO distributed agents
- If a task pulls in any of the above, it's out of scope — flag it, don't build it

## Layer separation (never cross these)
- Scanner modules → return `Finding` / `List[Finding]` only. Never touch SQLite,
  never calculate risk_score, never `print()`.
- `core/risk_scorer.py` → the ONLY file that calculates `risk_score`.
- `core/database.py` → the ONLY file allowed to `import sqlite3`.
- `cli.py` → Typer orchestration/display only. Zero business logic.

## Mandatory code rules
- Never `print()` directly — use Rich via `core/logger.py`
- Never `import sqlite3` outside `core/database.py`
- Never calculate `risk_score` outside `core/risk_scorer.py`
- Every active network action requires explicit `(y/n)` confirmation
- `restore.py` never deletes a file without verifying `session_id` ownership
- All functions fully typed (params + return)
- Scan functions always return `Finding` or `List[Finding]`
- Every module ships a pedagogical README.md (French)

## The Finding contract
Defined once in `core/finding.py` — do not redefine or duplicate it.
`risk_score` stays `None` until `risk_scorer.py` sets it.
`explanation` stays `None` until a matching entry exists in
`knowledge/vulnerabilities.json`.

## Before marking anything done
- No `print()` anywhere (grep-checkable)
- No `sqlite3` import outside `core/database.py` (grep-checkable)
- Unit test (nominal) + edge case + error case
- README.md present
- Confirm this doesn't silently expand scope beyond the ticket
